    "lawCode": "Amd §210-a, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S2487\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the education law, in relation to\nadmission requirements for graduate-level teacher and educational\nleader programs for certified teachers already holding a graduate\ndegree\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo provide that in-service teachers having completed a graduate\nprogram need not take the GRE.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1. Amends section 210-a of the education law to provide that\nthe graduate record examination (GRE) or substantially equivalent\nadmission examination requirement will not apply to certified teachers\nwho already hold a graduate degree when applying for a graduate-level\nteacher program.\n\nSection 2. Sets for the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nCurrently, the law requires that in order for any applicant to be\nadmitted to a graduate level teacher program, that applicant must have\ntaken the GRE or a substantially equivalent admission examination.\nThis does not account for teachers that are already certified who\ndecide to go back to get another certification and have already\nmatriculated through a graduate teaching program.  This is a\ncorrection to distinguish between in-service teachers and pre-service\nteachers. Teachers that are already in-service have already gone\nthrough a graduate program and thus should not need to take the GRE\nwhen they have already matriculated and decide to go back to receive\nmore certifications.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2016 S.7647\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
