    "lawCode": "Amd §210-a, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S2487A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to admission\nrequirements for graduate-level teacher and educational leader\nprograms for certified teachers already holding a graduate degree\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo provide that in-service teachers or school administrators having\ncompleted a graduate program need not take the GRE.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1. Amends section 210-a of the education law to provide that\nthe graduate record examination (GRE) or substantially equivalent\nadmission examination requirement will not apply to certified teachers\nor school administrators who already hold a graduate degree when\napplying for a graduate-level teacher program.\n\nSection 2. Sets forth the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nCurrently, the law requires that in order for any applicant to be\nadmitted to a graduate level teacher program, that applicant must have\ntaken the GRE or a substantially equivalent admission examination.\nThis does not account for teachers and school administrators that are\nalready certified who decide to go back to get another certification\nand have already matriculated through a graduate teaching program.\n\nThis is a correction to distinguish between in-service teacher and\npre-service teachers. Teachers and school administrators that are\nalready in-service and have already gone through a graduate program\nand thus should not need to take the GRE when they have already\nmatriculated and decide to go back to receive more certifications.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2016 S.7647.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
